3. Description of Mount Kailāsa; therein, description of the assembly of Śiva preceded by the description of the throne of Śiva; then, the Goddess’s hymn of praise to Śiva; dialogue between Śiva and Pārvatī; then, description of the yoga of divine manifestations addressed to Pārvatī by the glorious Śiva; then, description of the māhātmya of sacred fords; therein, especially the description of the māhātmya of the Prabhāsa sacred field; questioning of Śaṃkara by Pārvatī with the desire to hear the māhātmya of the sacred fords located in the Prabhāsa sacred field. 5 1
4. Statement to Pārvatī by Śaṃkara, upon being questioned by Pārvatī, regarding the boundary of the Prabhāsa sacred field, the dimensions of the sacred field, and the greatness of the sacred field;
description of the sequence of pilgrimage in the Prabhāsa sacred field; description of the pilgrimage according to the threefold division named Māheśvara, Vaiṣṇava, and Brāhma; therein, description of the three energies as well; description of the fruit of reciting [mantras] such as the Conqueror of Death; description of the attainment of liberation even by great sinners dwelling in the Prabhāsa sacred field; description of the māhātmya of the Śaiva attendants who guard the Prabhāsa sacred field. 8 1
